Summary
-------
PASS: typecheck, node tests (59/59), vitest (94/94 incl. 8 N16 UI tests),
      production build, scoped eslint (0/0), static greps.
FAIL: repo-wide lint (28 errors / 32 warnings, all pre-existing outside N16);
      `npm run check` cannot go green in this working tree until those
      unrelated files are fixed.
SKIP: none.
NOT_RUN: live T1/T2 (real top-up and real bill payment through Compose).
      Reasons: (a) this machine has no Docker/PostgreSQL/RabbitMQ, so the
      services cannot be started; (b) payment-service K13 still rejects
      PHONE_TOPUP / BILL_PAYMENT (payment.validation.ts only accepts CARD_TOPUP,
      BUS_TICKET, MOVIE_TICKET, TRAIN_TICKET, WALLET_TRANSFER), so a real
      checkout currently returns a definite 4xx and the order ends FAILED;
      (c) real PIN flow needs the K13 fix plus a seeded account (N20) and the
      real login (D17). Nothing here is claimed as PASS.

Risks / open items
------------------
- K13 gap: FE calls the agreed endpoints, but real checkout cannot succeed until
  payment-service accepts PHONE_TOPUP and BILL_PAYMENT. Recorded in
  docs/handover/utilities.md section 3.
- The 3% discount is stored on the order (discountAmount) but neither deducted
  from the charge nor credited to the wallet; the UI labels it as "ghi nhan"
  and charges the full denomination. Needs business confirmation.
- No provider catalogue endpoint: EVN/SAWACO/FPT are fixed sandbox codes in
  constants.ts because the backend only validates the string shape.
- Bill amount can only come from lookup; if the provider changes the bill
  between lookup and payment the backend returns BILL_AMOUNT_MISMATCH and the
  UI tells the user to look it up again.
- Gateway token: the FE relies on the existing lib/axios Bearer session; if the
  Gateway later requires a separate service token for /api/utilities it must be
  added in infrastructure, not in this feature.
- No preview build/push was performed; the branch is local only.
